{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abacusmodeling/LibRI/pulls/16","id":4986140703,"node_id":"PR_kwDOH8_nos8AAAABKTJ4Hw","html_url":"https://github.com/abacusmodeling/LibRI/pull/16","diff_url":"https://github.com/abacusmodeling/LibRI/pull/16.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/abacusmodeling/LibRI/pull/16.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abacusmodeling/LibRI/issues/16","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abacusmodeling/LibRI/pulls/16/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abacusmodeling/LibRI/pulls/16/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abacusmodeling/LibRI/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abacusmodeling/LibRI/issues/16/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abacusmodeling/LibRI/statuses/7025df62cc4d3c7a609d1acec1733ab4a95dc7fb","number":16,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix real-space symmetry filtering in GPU contractions","user":{"login":"Stardust0831","id":169599847,"node_id":"U_kgDOChvjZw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169599847?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831","html_url":"https://github.com/Stardust0831","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"GPU contractions with real-space symmetry can abort on a valid contraction label or lose contributions. GPU batching uses a different loop order from CPU contractions, so the shared symmetry callbacks must identify the actual output atom pair and relative cell at each call site.\n\nThe fix addresses three cases:\n\n- Add the missing GPU callback cases. Defer screening while only an intermediate atom is known, then check the output pair when both atoms are available.\n- Correct the argument order in four `a01b01_a2b2` contractions so the callback screens `(Aa01, Ab01)`.\n- In four `a01b2_a2b01` contractions, move the check inside the `Ab01` loop. Screening intermediate `Aa2` as an output atom had discarded valid terms from the sum.\n\nThe first two changes backport maki49's [initial fix](https://github.com/maki49/LibRI/commit/2f77684417313e78e2da67aeee2ebf9b44f1e9fe) and [extension](https://github.com/maki49/LibRI/commit/a0db48f56ffadf448c8057788df57562b42cd3c8), preserving authorship. The additional intermediate-sum correction has a numerical regression covering all 18 contraction labels and their combined sum, real/complex tensors, periodic cells, restricted/empty output and seeded accumulation. Its reference is an unrestricted CPU contraction with an independent mask on the final output keys.\n\nBoth CPU implementations retain their existing filtering rules. For the newly supported label/argument-type combinations, CPU calls different overloads; the symmetry delta leaves the CPU contraction loops unchanged.\n\nThis PR includes the accumulator and atom-list corrections from #15. [Symmetry changes relative to #15](https://github.com/Stardust0831/LibRI/compare/e72194dc104f47294c733ef314255ccec4995c11...7025df62cc4d3c7a609d1acec1733ab4a95dc7fb).\n\nThe original ABACUS failure was:\n\n```text\nterminate called after throwing an instance of 'std::invalid_argument'\n  what(): label a0b0_a1b1 error in .../Filter_Atom_Symmetry.h line 49\nSignal: Aborted (6)\n```\n\n[Original before/after records](https://github.com/Stardust0831/LibRI/blob/f9e6f9325794b63d26c07fadb708b11153ded8e4/gpu-symmetry/upstream/README.md) show four GPU-symmetry ABACUS cases aborting before the fix and passing after it. Among the 18 standalone contractions, the original version had 10 exceptions and four incorrect outputs; the two backports alone left four incorrect sums; the complete fix passes all 18.\n\nThe version merged with current `master` and #15 (`7025df6`) was validated again:\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Symmetry regression: CPU-only and GPU-enabled builds, real/complex tensors, 1/4 threads | All four runs pass, covering both CPU implementations and GPU execution |\n| Accumulation: float/double, real/complex, CPU-only/GPU-enabled, 1/4 threads | 16/16 runs pass |\n| Hartree reference, atom-list regressions, exchange/force/stress comparisons | 6/6 runs pass |\n| Complete ABACUS GPU build, including BSE | Pass |\n| ABACUS: five solver/RI/symmetry configurations × real/complex × one/two MPI ranks | 20/20 calculations pass repository checks and CPU/GPU comparisons |\n\nHardware: NVIDIA V100-SXM2 16 GB GPUs, GCC 13.3/OpenMP and DDLA v0.0.4/CUDA. ABACUS `b30b66a5a` uses only the test patch removing its GPU-symmetry rejection so execution reaches LibRI; no LibRI patches are applied. The ABACUS fixture has zero forces by symmetry, so it does not establish nonzero-force behavior. MAGMA, BSE numerical results and multi-node execution were not tested.\n\n[Complete merged-version build and runtime logs](https://github.com/Stardust0831/LibRI/blob/288a3d87fbd0a8cfe21718b72c32d7af6f121e44/merged-pr15-pr16-20261024/README.md). [Standalone reproduction](https://github.com/Stardust0831/LibRI/blob/7025df62cc4d3c7a609d1acec1733ab4a95dc7fb/unittests/gpu_symmetry/README.md). Related: deepmodeling/abacus-develop#8169.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-23T16:41:22Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T12:39:38Z","closed_at":"2026-10-24T12:39:37Z","merged_at":"2026-10-24T12:39:37Z","merge_commit_sha":"a0661cbb4b4f89ceeb23e040d49accb00943093f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Stardust0831:fix/gpu-symmetry-upstream","ref":"fix/gpu-symmetry-upstream","repo":{"id":1427953874,"node_id":"R_kgDOVRzY0g","name":"LibRI","full_name":"Stardust0831/LibRI","owner":{"login":"Stardust0831","id":169599847,"node_id":"U_kgDOChvjZw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169599847?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831","html_url":"https://github.com/Stardust0831","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stardust0831/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":true,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":null,"homepage":null,"language":"C++","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":0,"watchers_count":0,"watchers":0,"open_issues_count":3,"open_issues":3,"size":10521,"default_branch":"master","has_issues":false,"has_projects":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_downloads":false,"has_discussions":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pushed_at":"2026-11-03T09:50:40Z","created_at":"2026-10-21T06:11:26Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T07:07:59Z","allow_forking":true,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","li